  "description": "T1 Silver Birch: Fell to ground level / Section dismantle. \rJustification: while structurally stable at present, is causing ongoing and foreseeable issues due to its proximity to adjacent structures and underground services. The tree?s root system is contributing to surface distortion and is expected to increase in size, intensifying the risk of future structural and drainage interference. Its location restricts sustainable crown development and conflicts with overhead lines and pedestrian access, requiring frequent maintenance to mitigate nuisance. Removal will prevent further encroachment and associated damage while allowing for the establishment of more suitable, lower-water-demand planting within the streetscape. Given its constrained setting, removal represents a proportionate and preventative management measure consistent with good arboricultural practice."
